Both catalogs are complete. Bima's device holds his share of the Line 1 check
(Workflow A) and his own Line 2 (Workflow B). In this tutorial, Bima exports
his catalog and sends it to Heru, and a single merge on Heru's device combines
both workflows into one project.

## 1. Export Bima's catalog and start the merge

{% steps %}

1. **Bima:** Open the menu and select `Export project`. Leave `Light export`
   off and keep `TAR.GZ` (or choose `ZIP`) so the archive includes all records
   and any attached media. Select `Export project` and send the archive to
   Heru.
2. **Heru:** Open the menu, select `Merge project`, and pick Bima's archive
   with `Choose archive`. Confirm that `Project UUID` matches.
3. **Heru:** Select `Back up now`, tick the backup confirmation box, and select
   `Continue`.
4. **Heru:** Review each section (detailed below) and select `Merge project` at
   the end.

{% /steps %}

{% aside type="caution" title="Do not use Light export for the final merge" %}
`Light export` omits media files to keep transfers small over limited internet.
For a final merge, always leave `Light export` off and export a full `TAR.GZ`
or `ZIP` archive so photos, audio recordings, and other media are bundled with
the records.
{% /aside %}

{% aside type="tip" title="Merging catalogs from three or more lab members" %}
If additional lab members practiced as extra catalogers, repeat these steps
once for each teammate's export file. NAHPU merges each catalog cleanly into
the same project.
{% /aside %}

## 2. Review each merge section

The review steps show how cleanly the shared setup pays off:

- **Personnel:** All three team members appear as `Matched`, with zero new
  people. Bima's record is flagged `Conflict` only because his cataloger number
  changed (i.e., it is still `1` on Heru's device, while it advanced to `5` on
  Bima's after cataloging five specimens). For each cataloger, keep the version
  from the device they cataloged on: choose `Use imported` for Bima and leave
  `Keep current` for Heru.

{% devicepair
   tablet="app-screenshots/tutorials/teamwork/ipad-merge-personnel.webp"
   tabletAlt="NAHPU Merge project Personnel step on an iPad with 0 new, 3 matched, and 0 needing attention; Bima Sampel's conflict action set to Use imported"
   tabletLabel="Heru · iPad" /%}

- **Taxonomy:** Every taxon is matched.
- **Sites and Events:** Both workflows appear side by side. The shared Line 1
  records (Workflow A) are `Matched`, preserving one shared site catalog, while
  Bima's `TJBS-L2` site and event (Workflow B) are `New`. Keep `Keep current`
  for the matched records; the `Conflict` badge simply indicates that a
  matching record already exists on Heru's device.

{% devicepair
   tablet="app-screenshots/tutorials/teamwork/ipad-merge-sites.webp"
   tabletAlt="NAHPU Merge project Sites step on an iPad with 1 new, 2 matched, and 0 needing attention; TJHH-L1 and TJHH-P1 are listed as matches"
   tabletLabel="Heru · iPad" /%}

- **Specimens:** Bima's five records arrive as `New`, with no conflicts or
  items needing attention.

{% devicepair
   tablet="app-screenshots/tutorials/teamwork/ipad-merge-specimens.webp"
   tabletAlt="NAHPU Merge project Specimens step on an iPad with 5 new, 0 matched, and no conflicts"
   tabletLabel="Heru · iPad" /%}

## 3. Verify the merged project

Nothing is written to the database until the final `Merge project` button is
selected, and any error rolls the entire transaction back safely. Once the
merge finishes, open `Data table` under `Tools` on the dashboard: all ten
specimens, three sites, and three events now live together in one project.

{% devicepair
   tablet="app-screenshots/tutorials/teamwork/ipad-data-table-merged.webp"
   tabletAlt="NAHPU Data table on an iPad listing ten specimen records: Heru Handika 445 to 449 (Muridae), Bima Sampel 1 to 4 (Soricidae), and Bima Sampel 5 (Maxomys hylomyoides)"
   tabletLabel="Heru · iPad" /%}

{% aside type="tip" %}
For resolving conflicts and duplicate identifiers in larger team merges, see
[Merge a project and resolve conflicts](/en/how-to-recipes/protect-and-collaborate/merge-project/).
{% /aside %}

